PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: no
RATIONALE: Four YELLOW votes and one RED. The RED (theory_skeptic) is unrebutted and independently corroborated by novelty_killer ("mechanism-classic") and systems_reviewer ("standard speculative-execution tradeoff"). The analytic core p* = P/(S+P) with gain saturating at min(remaining-decode, tool-latency) while penalty grows linearly is the textbook speculative-execution cost model — substituting agent-step variable names does not create a new mechanism. The systems_reviewer's discovery of PASTE (arXiv 2603.18897v1) significantly raises the prior-art risk: PASTE targets the identical problem (serial LLM-tool loop in agents), performs speculative tool execution with predicted parameters, and reports real-trace results (48.5% task-completion reduction, 93.8% hit rate) — exactly the kind of empirical grounding CLAIM-0003 lacks. This was not cited in the packet.

I do NOT escalate to RED because: (1) the L0 methodology is genuinely sound — pre-registered, honest negative, MC-validated analytic model — and an honest conditional-negative is a legitimate research output; (2) the PASTE collision is not yet verified at mechanism-detail level (partial-arg-decode speculation vs pattern-level tool prediction may be distinguishable); (3) a viable path exists IF the claim is reframed as a measurement study and the prior-art collisions are cleared. But the path is narrow and the theory_skeptic's observation that the model UNDERSTATES the negative (w>1 excluded, p_correct likely anti-correlates with r, contention and batch effects ignored) means even the conditional-negative may be optimistic.

VERDICT: YELLOW — do not advance to GPU/real-trace pass until PASTE and LLMCompiler collisions are resolved via live retrieval. If collisions are cleared, the next pass must measure real p_correct (the single deciding unknown) and reframe the contribution as empirical characterization of a classic tradeoff in a new domain, not a novel mechanism. If PASTE subsumes the partial-arg case, escalate to RED/KILL.
